  "lineage": "Liturgical chanting of Vietnamese Mahayana Buddhism, in Sino-Vietnamese and vernacular Vietnamese, performed by monastics and lay congregations at pagodas for daily services, repentance rites, funerals and festivals. Recitation (tụng) is paced by the mõ wooden fish and punctuated by the bowl bell, while hymns (tán) are more melodic; Huế is known for its Buddhist ritual-music tradition, and the Plum Village communities have carried recorded Vietnamese chant abroad. The temple-bell card stands in for the chuông bowl bell.",
